cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. It is an improved version of a fork of EvoMaster; please also cite the upstream framework."
title: "SeqOpt: an agentic C-source optimization loop for HMMER jackhmmer with paired-measurement acceptance"
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
type: software
abstract: >-
  An optimization loop in which a language-model agent proposes patches to the C
  sources of HMMER's jackhmmer iterative search. Every candidate is screened in a
  two-stage evaluation (smoke then full) on a fixed query set against UniRef90
  and scored against the SCOPe lineage under hard TP/FP non-regression gates.
  Acceptance decisions are backed by a comparability fingerprint, paired
  interleaved re-measurement of the current best, a zero-effect noise-floor
  calibration, and decoy probes that are known to add only work. This repository
  also documents one verified case in which such a decoy probe was accepted as a
  speedup, which is recorded as a known limitation rather than a result.
keywords:
  - AI for Science
  - protein sequence search
  - HMMER
  - jackhmmer
  - profile hidden Markov models
  - large language model agent
  - automated algorithm optimization
  - measurement reliability
  - reproducible benchmarking
authors:
